--[[
    TextBoxTranslations
game.ReplicatedStorage.Modules.Client.Localization.TextBoxTranslations
    Manual translation dictionary for TextBox.Text values, used in place of the
    real LocalizationTable/Translator for these specific objects.

    Why: testing showed Translator:Translate() / FormatByKey() correctly update
    a TextLabel's .Text, but the same calls did not visibly change a TextBox's
    .Text even with a matching CSV entry - so these are looked up here and
    written to .Text directly instead, driven off the player's locale
    (TranslationHelper.GetPlayerLanguage()).

    Keyed by the exact English source text, then by language ("es", "fr", "pt").
    A key/language combination that's missing just means the object keeps its
    original English text - TranslationHelper.TranslateFromDictionary() never
    errors and never returns an empty replacement.

    Fill these in from the existing CSV localization table (same source
    strings, same translations - just duplicated here for the objects this
    applies to). "Build #{number1}" keeps Roblox's {number1} parameter syntax;
    LocalizationHandler substitutes the real number itself.
]]
return {
	["Enter ID#"] = {
		es = "Ingresa el ID#",
		fr = "Entrez l’ID#",
		pt = "Digite o ID#",
	},

	["BORN TO SING"] = {
		es = "NACER PARA CANTAR",
		fr = "NÉ POUR CHANTER",
		pt = "NASCIDO PARA CANTAR",
	},

	["Build #{number1}"] = {
		es = "Construcción #{number1}",
		fr = "Construction #{number1}",
		pt = "Construção #{number1}",
	},
}
